Z||000010||Songman||08-21-2001||06:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SteveJ:<BR><B>I love it.<P>Isn't XP the version where they want people to register it over the net or it quits working after 60 days?<P>[This message has been edited by SteveJ (edited 08-21-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not when you have the crack!<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beer_stud_21:<BR><B>Hey Songman,<P>I'm a mac man myself and have always had people me how Macs and iMacs in particular look like toys.  But from the screen shots of WinXP I sure think Microsoft should have named WindowsXP WindowsPLAYSKOOL  or WindowsXP.O.S...  hehe<P>-marlin</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Marlin...<P>I started out on Macs in the graphic design world just after the first came out. I've always loved them. They sure don't look like toys to me! If I were still doing graphic design I would still be using a Mac!<P>I was never afraid to jump in and grab the new systems released for the Macs either. I remember when System 7 came out and people were scared to death of it! I loved it from day one!<P>I haven't even seen XP yet other than the disc I have. I have heard it looks cartoonish but is very efficient, has tons of things built into it that you had to add in before, and is very unlikely to have problems with crashes. Of course, I never have crashes with Windows 2000 either. I'm just going to do an upgrade instead of a clean install. I will still be able to choose either 2000 or XP to start up from and I can always go back to 2000 if I don't like XP.<P>And btw.. one of these days when I am not throwing so much money away on my cars I will have a G4 Mac sitting here beside my PC!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
